  "id": "COMPOUND:16764 - PROTEIN:5864",
  "verbalization": "Iriskumaonin methyl ether is implicated in the biological activity of U373 MG through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Iriskumaonin methyl ether acts as a target for Raji cells, which in turn are targeted by multiple compounds, including Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside and (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one. These compounds all ultimately target U373 MG, indicating a shared mechanism of action involving the cell line Raji. The presence of multiple pathways converging on U373 MG suggests that Iriskumaonin methyl ether may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the Raji cell line, potentially through the activation of downstream signaling pathways or the modulation of cellular processes that are critical for the survival or proliferation of U373 MG. The integrated evidence highlights a potential role for Iriskumaonin methyl ether in the regulation of Raji cells, which in turn influence U373 MG through a complex network of molecular interactions.",
